#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""docklet: a dock for river + rivermonad, in the family of spacelet,
locklet, waymobar and bgmonad.

  docklet            start the dock (it stays running)
  docklet toggle     show it now, or hide it again (for a key)
  docklet quit       stop it
  docklet --help

A tab that grows out of an edge of the screen with the applications that
are running and, before them, the ones pinned to it. It is hidden: push
the pointer against the edge and it slides out, and it goes away a moment
after the pointer leaves it.

  click          go to the application's window (again: its next window),
                 or start it when it is not running
  middle click   a new window of it
  right click    a menu: its windows, new window, the actions of its
                 desktop file, pin it to the dock or unpin it, close it
  drag           an icon onto another one to reorder the pinned ones
                 (dragging one that is not pinned pins it there)

The windows come from rivermonad's IPC socket (rivermonad >= 0.4.3); the
icons and names from the applications' desktop files.

Settings: ~/.config/docklet/config.json (the pinned applications are kept
there too); ~/.config/docklet/style.css is loaded after the built-in style
(GTK CSS) to restyle it.

Needs python-gobject, GTK 4, gtk4-layer-shell and rivermonad.
"""
import json
import math
